                <pb facs="0562" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg482"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Sickles to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July 3,
                        1901</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 512.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    to-day of your telegraphic instruction in reply to my cablegram of the 30th
                    instant.</p>
                <p>The purport of your cablegram has been repeated at once by wire to the
                    consul-general at Barcelona.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stanton Sickles</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chargé d’Affaires ad interim.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
